    },
    {
      "id": "8zkna21",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Neutralization Reaction"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gatuxmt",
      "content": "Neutralization is the reaction between an acid and a base to form salt and water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hxnk7mf",
      "content": "Example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jdnow2u",
      "content": "HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H₂O"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6ki9uw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "r3ot3cz",
      "content": "• Salts are ionic compounds formed from neutralization reactions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vvn94o5",
      "content": "• They may be acidic, basic or neutral."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3pa6v8i",
      "content": "• Examples include sodium chloride, copper sulfate and ammonium chloride."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Indicator Color Changes: Phenolphthalein turns pink in basic solutions and remains colorless in acidic solutions; Methyl orange turns red in acid and yellow in base.",
        "Plaster of Paris (CaSO4·½H2O) hardens into Gypsum (CaSO4·2H2O) upon mixing with water.",
        "Strength of acids and bases depends on the degree of ionization in water, not merely on concentration.",
        "Antacids like Milk of Magnesia [Mg(OH)2] are weak bases used to neutralize excess stomach acidity."
      ],
      "id": "gzrlmau"
    },
    {
      "id": "e6frfys",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10. Uses of Acids, Bases and Salts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mzja076",
      "content": "• Acids are used in batteries and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cvhrtnr",
      "content": "• Bases are used in soap making and cleaning agents."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2ozf5ca",
      "content": "• Salts are used in food preservation and fertilizers."
    },
    {
      "id": "scpz49q",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "80uzew7",
      "content": "• Acids produce hydrogen ions in water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "17wxdv9",
      "content": "• Bases produce hydroxide ions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wfnar1c",
      "content": "• pH scale ranges from 0 to 14."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cgcb3ha",
      "content": "• Neutralization produces salt and water."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}